WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.880
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:11.990
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:17.560
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:26.330
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.080
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.550
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.410
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.150
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.820
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.500
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:01.160
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.540
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:12.180
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:17.090
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:22.320
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:32.430
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:37.170
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.910
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.510
"Raizo Shiranagatani"

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:51.640
What do you say to 50 million?
"Raizo Shiranagatani"

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.680
If it'll free me from the
curse of the Blade Children,

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.420
"Takako Adachi - Translator"

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.710
it's more than worth it.
"Takako Adachi - Translator"

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.760
<i>Don't you die on me, Sonobe.</i>

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.060
<i>You're the only clue we have as
to Kiyotaka-san's whereabouts!</i>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.120
The...Manor...

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.470
The Manor...of Death...

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.100
The Manor of Death?

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.670
"The Manor of Death"

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.180
Narumi here.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.920
A murder at the Manor of Death?!

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.820
That's not all.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.050
The Manor of Death that Sonobe mentioned,

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.610
that's the house where that
Sayoko Shiranagatani girl lives.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.460
<i>First she's attacked by Sonobe,</i>

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.030
<i>and now there's a murder at her home...</i>

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.090
Is it just a coincidence?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.740
<i>The victim was Takako Adachi-san,
a translator.</i>

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.210
She was apparently here last
night reading specialized books

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.380
<i>that Shiranagatani-san keeps in his library.</i>

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:45.050
She appears to have died of brain
damage caused by a blow to the head.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:48.250
Basically, the victim died
after she hit her head

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.090
against the corner of this
chair for whatever reason.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.790
You were all in your rooms at her
estimated time of death of 2:00 AM?

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.800
"Reiko Hatsuyama - Servant"

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.430
"Sayoko Shiranagatani - Raizo's niece"
"Kei Shiranagatani - Raizo's granddaughter"

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.270
We were sound asleep.
"Sayoko Shiranagatani - Raizo's niece"
"Kei Shiranagatani - Raizo's granddaughter"

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.630
"Raizo Shiranagatani - Mansion's owner"

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.140
There's a possibility it could
have been an accidental death...

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.010
Would she leave that behind
if that were the case?

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.310
Good point...

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.780
Who was the first to find her?

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.910
Me, Kei.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:21.680
<i>But Sayoko-chan was in front of
the library before me this morning.</i>

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:27.020
The door was locked so I couldn't go in...

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:32.160
<i>Sayoko-sama stops by the library
before breakfast every morning.</i>

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:32.930
You too?

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.730
I just came to borrow a book for class.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.200
<i>When I got here, Sayoko-chan
was in front of the door.</i>

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.310
She said the door was locked,
so I peeked inside the keyhole.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.150
I saw a key was inserted
from the other side,

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.380
so I pushed it out with a pen I had.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.220
And then...

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.820
Afterward, you explained the situation
to the servant, Reiko Hatsuyama,

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.760
who was in the dining room,

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.660
and then she opened the
door with a spare key?

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.630
I'm in charge of all the spare keys, so...

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.570
Are there any other keys to that room?

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.570
No, just the two.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:14.340
Who confirmed that she was dead?

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.510
That would be me.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:21.450
<i>Where were you at the time,
Raizo Shiranagatani-san?</i>

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.580
In my room.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.650
I informed him of the situation
only after everything was over.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.290
He's not in good health, you see...

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:33.020
Are you ill?

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.250
I'm at that age.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.950
<i>Was that you playing the
piano just now, Narumi-san?</i>

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.490
It was, wasn't it?

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.760
You half asleep or something?

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.360
Fine, then! If you're
going to be like that,

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.900
then I won't tell you the
special information I have!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.140
I don't really care...

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.810
<i>Even if it's about Sayoko
Shiranagatani-san?</i>

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:24.810
Did something happen to her?!

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:28.580
Oh? I thought you didn't care?

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:32.250
You're meaner than you look,
you know that?

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:37.050
I'll tell you about it if
you play the piano for me.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:40.490
I've given up the piano...

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.490
Given up?

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.730
What do you say to lunch instead?

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.000
I have some croissants I
just baked this morning...

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.990
You made them yourself?!

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.140
A warded lock...Another sticky
affair this is going to be...

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.210
It's made of a copper alloy...

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.980
And with one as complicated as this,

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.280
duplication would be nearly impossible.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.450
But why do you suppose they used a key lock

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:08.290
if the door could be locked from
the inside with this deadbolt?

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.120
The deadbolt can't be
manipulated from the outside.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:13.920
And with the key inside the keyhole...

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.090
...the deadbolt can't move because
of the way it's constructed.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:20.630
The killer committed a murder
in a completely-locked room.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.200
I see!

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.030
And then there's that dying message...

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.040
What do you suppose it means?

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:31.410
Finding that out is the most
important thing right now...

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:36.250
That appears to be the
last book the victim read.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.480
We found her fingerprints on it...

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.490
What's this?!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.150
I'm so happy!

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.590
This croissant with its butter fragrance
and this heart-warming café au lait!

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:50.660
<i>You can really feel your kindness
when you eat it, Narumi-san!</i>

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:54.530
You must really think a lot of your sister!

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.600
So how about telling me now?

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.670
Telling you what?

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:58.600
Ugh!

00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.340
Later.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.070
Okay, okay!

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.610
<i>I'll tell you the latest
news about Sayoko-san!</i>

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.980
Apparently last night,

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:09.980
<i>a murder took place in a locked
room at Sayoko-san's house!</i>

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:11.880
A murder in a locked room?!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:17.620
<i>But it's too much of a coincidence for
her to be attacked by Sonobe-sensei</i>

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.990
and then for a murder to take
place at her home, don't you think?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.560
The Blade Children...

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.770
I'm sorry to have to say this,

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.140
but judging from this
mansion's security system,

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:37.910
it seems unlikely that this
was the work of an outsider.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.340
In other words...

00:08:39.340 --> 00:08:42.510
<i>Raizo Shiranagatani-san,
head of the household...</i>

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.120
<i>Sayoko-san, his granddaughter...</i>

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.280
<i>Kei-san, her cousin...</i>

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.590
<i>And Reiko Hatsuyama-san, the housekeeper...</i>

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.590
We will continue our investigation
with you all as suspects.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.090
Wataya.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:53.960
Right.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:58.300
Our examination found that none of
the victim's things were damaged,

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.270
so this was clearly not a robbery.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.200
In addition, we found no signs
of a struggle on her body,

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.160
so the killer was likely someone
who approached her casually.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:12.440
I assume you all know
what a dying message is?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.210
On the verge of death,
the victim left a symbol

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.520
meant to be a clue to
the killer's identity.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:21.890
...The square whirlpool-like
character next to the body.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:25.790
And this was the last
book the victim read.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.230
There's a character on this
that looks very similar

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.720
to what the victim left behind.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:34.830
According to this book, this
character stands for lightning,

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:37.470
and is called the "Rai" character.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.770
What do you think about this,

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.510
<i>Raizo Shiranagatani-san?</i>

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:42.490
<i>"Rai"
Raizo Shiranagatani-san?</i>

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.540
I doubt it's a coincidence.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.520
It's the same character as the one in
the book she read just before dying.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.450
Ayumu!

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.090
Not you again!

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:58.760
Sorry for listening in
on your conversation!

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.420
Not you too!

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:04.430
We're in the middle of a police
investigation! Please leave!

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.160
The Blade Children...

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.730
What are you doing?

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.600
It's on your mind too, isn't it?

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:17.070
You know something, don't you?

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:20.140
Raizo Shiranagatani...
Former company president...

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.910
Everyone in the industry
was talking about it

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:27.280
after you made a fortune in a single
generation but then suddenly retired

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:30.590
immediately after taking
in your granddaughter, huh?

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.890
Where did you get that information?!

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:34.560
From me!

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.430
And then this latest incident...

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:42.530
The Blade Children have something
to do with it all, don't they?

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:49.600
Uncouth little scoundrel...

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:01.280
Say, what are the Blade Children?

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.480
<i>Narumi-san?</i>

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.200
<i>It sounds like Sayoko Shiranagatani-san
started going back to school</i>

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:18.800
this afternoon!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.970
You have a really sharp ear, don't you?

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.440
I'm head of the newspaper
for a reason, you know!

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.810
There's nothing I don't hear about!

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.850
I hear you have dirt on
all the teachers too!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:31.910
Dirt?! It's just information, that's all!

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.790
Sorry to interrupt...

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.620
<i>Sayoko-san?!</i>

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.220
The victim, Takako Adachi...

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.230
Apparently she had recently
talked to the family doctor

00:11:42.230 --> 00:11:45.100
about acquiring a large sum
of money or something!

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.160
To the doctor?

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.170
She apparently suffered
from a heart disease,

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:52.000
and even the slightest thing
would cause an intense attack.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.140
Acquiring a large sum of money...

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.770
Blackmail?

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.040
Maybe she was blackmailing Raizo
Shiranagatani?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.240
"Newspaper Office"

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.310
"Newspaper Office"
When I was 12,

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:02.250
I evidently fell down
a flight of stairs

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.520
and lost my memory from the shock.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:12.720
But there's not a single old picture
left, so I don't know the truth...

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:15.930
I don't feel unsatisfied
with my current family.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:17.830
But still...

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.700
You have been involved in
strange incidents recently...

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:24.270
So what did you want to ask me?

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.040
What are the Blade Children?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:32.940
<i>Adachi-san told me earlier that
she wanted to tell me about them.</i>

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.280
But I never had a chance
to find out anything;

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:39.750
she had a bad heart so she
was rarely ever around...

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.190
Her heart?

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.050
...Heart...

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:47.630
Please! If you know anything
about the Blade Children, tell me!

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:51.490
It might help me learn about my past!

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.930
Without my memory, there's
no sense of reality for me.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:59.640
Everything around me seems fake...

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:04.240
<i>Fake? Yes, I feel it too.</i>

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:07.680
<i>Why does something feel out of place?</i>

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.910
<i>It's like there's something missing...</i>

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.210
<i>That's it!</i>

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:21.420
<i>There was a very specific
thing missing there.</i>

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.290
<i>The truth has been played.</i>

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:30.000
The key to unlocking that
sealed room was time.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.200
Time?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.540
Yes. The killer used the time and
space, which were our blind spots,

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.680
to create a completely sealed room.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:40.880
But the field of vision through
the keyhole is very narrow.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.750
There would've been plenty of
blind spots for the killer to hide.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.120
So the killer was still in the room?!

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:51.420
Yes! And when Sayoko and
Kei went to get Reiko,

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:54.590
the killer undid the inner
deadbolt and left the room.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:58.030
Then the killer closed the door again,

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.630
and then put a string or
something through the keyhole,

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:03.630
which was the only opening
to the sealed room...

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:06.640
...and locked the deadbolt.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:08.070
So that means the killer is...

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:14.480
<i>Raizo Shiranagatani-san!</i>

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.000
You are the killer!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:22.850
I see. That is a very interesting
judgment you have there...

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.960
But I do have one observation.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.020
For such a hurriedly-constructed trick,

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:30.830
it was really lucky the killer had the
foresight to have a string on hand.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:33.460
You always have one with you:

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:36.970
...that watch strap of yours!

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:41.540
Yes. According to your theory,
I do appear to be the killer...

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.680
Excellent work, Assistant Inspector!

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.040
But he couldn't have done it.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.680
Detective...

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:54.750
Unfortunately, I could not
have been the killer.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:58.590
As you can see, I am completely blind.

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.890
<i>No way!</i>

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:03.950
So it is a talking watch.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:09.370
I had suspected it was ever
since I first saw it.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:10.800
Are you butting in again?!

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:15.910
If this sealed-room murder had gone
exactly as the killer had planned,

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:17.340
there would've been no incident,

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:20.580
and the truth would have
remained in the darkness...

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:23.780
However, a number of circumstances
prevented that from happening,

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:27.790
and as a result, we were
given two definitive clues...

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.350
The first is that dying message, huh?

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:31.360
Yeah.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:35.190
And the second is that something
that should be here isn't here.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.490
Something that should be here?

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.130
The victim had a weak heart, right?

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.200
That's right! Her medicine!

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:46.600
She had a disease that caused
life-threatening heart attacks.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.110
So then why was the medicine to
prevent that missing from her things?

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:53.640
Because the killer had removed them
from her belongings in advance.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:58.950
With the intention of murdering her
by causing her to have a heart attack!

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.640
This was the killer's aim.

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.150
The reason being that at that very instant,

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:34.550
the isolated room and the outside
were connected by the single key.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.320
The killer sent electricity through
it using a stun gun or something!

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:41.420
And that's why that lightning
character was there!

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:48.730
Most likely, she wanted to
convey the lightning-like shock...

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:53.170
And while suffering from an attack,
the victim searched her handbag.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.070
Unable to find the medicine,
she fell lifeless.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.370
Or she should have.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:02.680
But now comes the killer's miscalculation...

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:14.760
The victim fell over due to the pain
and received fatal damage to the brain.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.790
But in her semi-conscious state,

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:22.230
she wrote that message in
retaliation against the killer.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:26.900
Wait a minute! That means anyone
of them could've done it!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:29.340
At this point, yes.

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:34.110
But the melody of logic
always plays the truth.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.980
The truth about the killer, in this case!

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:43.950
In order to have the police simply
call it a heart attack death,

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.720
the killer would have planned
to put the medicine back

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.390
with the rest of the victim's belongings.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:51.830
That chance was lost when she died

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:54.670
of a completely different cause, though.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.930
If we assume this,

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.340
then the killer was someone in a position

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.740
to unlock the door with a duplicate key

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.880
and get extremely close to the
body to doctor up the scene...

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.070
In other words... You!

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.290
I don't know if it was your
boss's orders or not,

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:20.090
but you were the only one who
could've actually done it.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:21.350
<i>Reiko-san?</i>

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:24.760
Detective...

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:27.460
Please forgive me.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.500
This was all my responsibility.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.240
<i>Raizo-sama knew nothing about it.</i>

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.970
Why'd you do it?!

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:38.640
My parents died in a factory accident.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.240
On top of that, I was
blamed for the accident

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.480
and my life fell apart all around me...

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:48.850
<i>The one who saved me from
that was Raizo-sama.</i>

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.420
Protecting him and this mansion

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:54.960
is the only way for me
to repay his kindness.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:58.400
Takako Adachi mentioned something
about the Blade Children,

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:02.000
<i>which made Raizo-sama and
Sayoko-sama suffer for a while now.</i>

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:07.870
In order to protect this house,
I couldn't let Adachi or Sonobe go!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.070
Sonobe? You don't mean...

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:13.240
You're also the one who attacked Sonobe?!

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:17.880
I know what I did is unforgivable.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.280
<i>But Sayoko-sama was in grave danger
unless somebody did something!</i>

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:24.080
This was the only choice there was...

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:30.890
As for what the Blade Children
are, I myself do not really know...

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:34.500
But they apparently gnawed away at Sayoko.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.430
What do you mean?

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.240
Ten years ago, my daughter absconded

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.140
and suddenly brought Sayoko back here.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:44.980
My daughter died of an
illness immediately afterward,

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:47.280
so I was never able to ask her anything.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:50.310
After that, I raised Sayoko myself,

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.850
but she was always scared of something

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:56.650
and would mutter how she
was a cursed child...

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:59.520
And then there were these
incidents, to top it all off...

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:03.860
Does she really have
that terrible of a past?

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:07.600
She's still just a child,
for goodness' sake...

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:12.140
Even after all this, I still
don't know anything about my past...

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:16.070
There's still a chance you'll
regain your memories naturally.

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:19.110
Though your past self
might not want that...

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:22.450
But this fake life...

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.880
There's someone who sacrificed
herself to protect that fake life.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.560
Is your current life really a fake?

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:37.390
You should think long and
hard about that on your own.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.300
<i>Great work, Narumi-san!</i>

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.100
You figured out another
trick in no time flat!

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:46.660
You're too amazing!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:55.050
<i>I still don't know anything at all...</i>

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:58.610
<i>What exactly are the Blade Children?</i>

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:12.690
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:19.390
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:37.550
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:43.190
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:49.090
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:55.670
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:55.670 --> 00:22:01.410
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:06.610
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:12.450
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:24.060
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.830
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:36.140
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:44.570
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:46.580
Now what's going on?!

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:49.280
It sure is thrilling and mysterious!

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:52.820
Your eyes are stuck on
the Spiral, aren't they?!

00:22:52.820 --> 00:22:56.320
The highlights of the third episode
include a beautiful piano melody

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:58.290
and a little turtle's monologue!

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:00.660
Turtles...Turtles!

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:02.760
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:04.190
The Cursed Children

00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:05.860
Don't miss next week's episode!

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:08.090
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
